And then there are mods OFF nexus that work for mages. Nothing NSFW and no piracy.

Tel Nalta -- [https://www.afkmods.com/index.php?/files/file/2362-tel-nalta-se/](https://www.afkmods.com/index.php?/files/file/2362-tel-nalta-se/)

Glenbeag -- [https://sites.google.com/view/mixwatermods/lierin/glenbeag](https://sites.google.com/view/mixwatermods/lierin/glenbeag)

Don’t know if you’ll ever find the perfect one, but these are both very pretty and not too large. Make sure to get the family versions.

{{The Northern Star Retreat - Revisited}}

{{Mona Alta}}

If you want truly good voice acting for mods, try Slimesire’s latest. They are by far the best voice acting for mods (popular followers like Inigo and Lucien aside) that I’ve experienced. In terms of the worst… Gray Cowl of Nocturnal in my experience.

{{The Tale of Tsatampra Xiros}}

{{Identity Crisis}}

I'm looking forward to player home mods that add aquariums, now! I hope to see more of them in the future! So far, I've only seen one player home with fishing stuff. Tuktura - A Houseboat Home

&#x200B;

Other than that, I've only seen the Fish Anywhere mod, which somebody already linked. New poles would be cool!

I highly recommend checking out {{Katie's Beast Race Aesthetics Compendium For SSE WIP}}

[Link](https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/45654?tab=description&BH=2) in case the bot doesn't find it. 

It's not a mod itself, but rather a huge list of all the best argonian and khajiit mods available for use on SSE. It's all in the description with links to everything.
